.TH timespec_get 3 2026\-02\-11 "Linux man\-pages (未リリース)" 
.SH 名前
timespec_get, timespec_getres \- ISO C interface to clock and time functions
.SH ライブラリ
標準 C ライブラリ (\fIlibc\fP,\~\fI\-lc\fP)
.SH 書式
.nf
\fB#include <time.h>\fP
.P
\fBint timespec_get(struct timespec *\fP\fIres\fP\fB, int \fP\fIbase\fP\fB);\fP
\fBint timespec_getres(struct timespec *\fP\fItp\fP\fB, int \fP\fIbase\fP\fB);\fP
.fi
.P
.RS -4
glibc 向けの機能検査マクロの要件 (\fBfeature_test_macros\fP(7)  参照):
.RE
.P
\fBtimespec_get\fP(), \fBTIME_UTC\fP:
.nf
    _ISOC11_SOURCE
.fi
.P
\fBtimespec_getres\fP(), \fBTIME_MONOTONIC\fP, \fBTIME_ACTIVE\fP,
\fBTIME_THREAD_ACTIVE\fP:
.nf
    _ISOC23_SOURCE
.fi
.SH 説明
The \fBtimespec_get\fP()  function stores the current time, based on the
specified time base, in the \fBtimespec\fP(3type)  structure pointed to by
\fIres\fP.
.P
The \fBtimespec_getres\fP()  function stores the resolution of times retrieved
by \fBtimespec_get\fP()  with the specified time base in the \fBtimespec\fP(3type)
structure pointed to by \fItp\fP, if \fItp\fP is non\-NULL.  For a particular time
base, the resolution is constant for the lifetime of the calling process.
.P
The time base \fIbase\fP is one of the following:
.TP 
\fBTIME_UTC\fP
A system\-wide time base that measures real (i.e., wall\-clock) time.  The
time and resolution in this time base are the same as those retrieved by
\fIclock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME,\~res)\fP and
\fIclock_getres(CLOCK_REALTIME,\~tp)\fP, respectively.
.TP 
\fBTIME_MONOTONIC\fP
A time base that measures time since an unspecified point in the past, where
the time within a process will not decrease even if the system's real time
clock is set or adjusted.  The time and resolution in this time base are the
same as those retrieved by \fIclock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC,\~res)\fP and
\fIclock_getres(CLOCK_MONOTONIC,\~tp)\fP, respectively.
.TP 
\fBTIME_ACTIVE\fP
A process\-specific time base that measures CPU time consumed by the calling
process.  The time and resolution in this time base are the same as those
retrieved by \fIclock_gettime(CLOCK_PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID,\~res)\fP and
\fIclock_getres(CLOCK_PROCESS_CPUTIME_ID,\~tp)\fP, respectively.
.TP 
\fBTIME_THREAD_ACTIVE\fP
A thread\-specific time base that measures CPU time consumed by the calling
thread.  The time and resolution in this time base are the same as those
retrieved by \fIclock_gettime(CLOCK_THREAD_CPUTIME_ID,\~res)\fP and
\fIclock_getres(CLOCK_THREAD_CPUTIME_ID,\~tp)\fP, respectively.
.SH 返り値
\fBtimespec_get\fP()  returns the nonzero \fIbase\fP if it is a supported time
base and the current time was successfully retrieved, or 0 otherwise.
.P
\fBtimespec_getres\fP()  returns the nonzero \fIbase\fP if it is a supported time
base, or 0 otherwise.
